\description{
Trial-level data from the three experiments of Yurovsky & Frank (2015), \emph{An
integrative account of constraints on cross-situational learning},
Cognition, 145, 53-62 (\doi{10.1016/j.cognition.2015.07.013}), from
\url{https://github.com/dyurovsky/XSIT-MIN}. Adults on Mechanical Turk heard each
of 8 novel words twice. On a word's first (exposure) trial they saw several
novel objects and guessed its referent; its second (test) trial came some
trials later and contained one object from the exposure trial among novel
ones: the one they chose (Same), one they didn't (Switch), or one they
didn't with a new word (New Label). Above-chance choices on Switch trials
show that learners remember more than their single hypothesis.
}
